=======================================================================================================
FRAME GEOMETRY SURVEY + PROBE CALIBRATION  -  21/08/2026
=======================================================================================================
Session record. Covers Z probe trigger height, the P5/P9 resolution, a bed.g
motor-order bug, and a full gantry geometry survey cross-checked against a
Mitutoyo DTI. Ends with a shim schedule and an order list.

Machine state during all of this: damaged/temporary granite slab fitted, no bed
heater attached, hotend PT1000 still failed (so everything COLD). Replacement
slab on order.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. HEADLINE FINDINGS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
a) The right Y rail sits LOW at the rear by 0.42mm (measured across a 380mm
   probe span; 0.61mm at the actual 550mm rail spacing). Front rails are level
   to 0.022mm. This is the dominant geometric error on the machine.
   Cause: assembly, not a loose joint - see section 5.

b) Both Y rails bow upward mid-span by ~0.2mm. This is COMMON MODE (left +0.193,
   right +0.217) so it produces no beam roll. Leave it - mesh cancels it exactly.

c) The X beam is good: 0.082mm bow over 380mm = 0.21mm/m. Do not touch it.

d) The ALPS probe is ACCURATE. Mesh and DTI agree to rms 0.019mm across 360mm.
   The earlier suspicion that the bowl was probe compliance is DISPROVEN.

e) G31 trigger height was badly wrong: was +0.7 (placeholder), measured -0.025.
   Wrong in sign as well as magnitude.

